========================================================================================================
4.  CONTOUR COST OF AN EXTRA SINGULAR POINT
========================================================================================================
  If the added function is singular at y = q (nontrivial monodromy) then phi factors
  through the universal cover of P^1 minus the enlarged singular set, which is contained
  in P^1 \ {0, q, infinity}; hence  |phi'(0)| <= 16|q|  (256|q| if the Z/2 descent is
  available with q as the outer point).  q = 1/Lambda for the decayer's own variable.
  family                     |q|=1/Lambda  log(16|q|)  log(256|q|)  CDT tau  shortfall
  conductor 3,  alpha=2        9.7653e-04     -4.1589      -1.3863   4.2355    -5.6218
  conductor 6,  alpha=1/4      2.6849e+04     12.9706      15.7432   4.2355    11.5077
  conductor 6,  alpha=1/2      1.5892e+03     10.1436      12.9162   4.2355     8.6807
